{
 "what": "R58 step 7, no step at a tile swap (fix round of Task 32, after the review's I1 and I2): the mean absolute difference of a film frame to the frame before it at each tile swap of the bend, against the mean of its two neighbours' (per 16.7 ms of film time, floored at 0.2 grey levels), home to the portfolio at 1440 by 900, three runs, with the same change with no bend (the tab's own rule `ft-glass-bend=off`) as the control. Made by make-tile-swaps.mjs and sum-tile-swaps.mjs, under the gate lock, on the production build of R58.4 (early step 0.0125).",
 "target": "ratio at most 1.5 (or 1.5 times the control's ratio there, floored at 1) at every swap",
 "audit_fix": "The first round's audit gave the recorder the animation's LINEAR progress (the CSS animation's timing function is the keyframes' own easing, so getComputedTiming().progress is the time fraction) and never applied the app's ease, so every tile, front and bend in the first record was wrong (labels repeated). It now applies the ease before the front and the bend, clamps the ladder as pickBendTile does and checks itself: `strictlyIncreasing` is true for every run below (the recovered tile numbers rise at every swap; `skippedTiles` lists where one frame moved two tiles). The first round's numbers, and Ruling R126 which rested on them, are withdrawn.",
 "tiles": "64 bend tiles: tiles 0 to 35 are the early ones, fronts -0.25 to 0.1875 every 0.0125 (BEND_EARLY_STEP), tiles 36 to 63 the ladder from HAND_OVER 0.2 at steps of 8% of the radius (TILE_RATIO 1.08). A swap's tile number is the real index into BEND_TILES.",
 "result": "Of the 48 swaps a run (tile 9, front -0.14, to tile 60, front 1.23; the numbers of the ones with the bend under 0.05 are in `swaps` but not in the worst), all are within 1.5 of their neighbours' change in all three runs but these: (1) tile 23, front 0.042, bend 0.91: ratio 3.6 to 4.0 in every run (3.45 at tile 24 in run 1, one frame later): NOT a tile swap, see `half_pixel_step` below; (2) tile 58, front 1.049, ratio 1.54 and 1.55 in runs 2 and 3 (0.84 in run 1; 1.58 to 1.68 in the strip's film and the counter-experiment's; the control there is 0.8 to 1.2; the step is 0.18 to 0.24 grey levels of 255 over its neighbours: invisible, the change itself is under 0.5 a frame there); (3) run 1 only, tiles 37 to 39 (fronts 0.22 to 0.26): ratio 1.70 with the control's own frames at the same time showing 2.0 (a screencast timing slip: runs 2 and 3 read 0.99 to 1.15 at the same swaps).",
 "half_pixel_step": {
  "finding": "The one-frame step at 'tile 23' is a step of the whole page, not of the bend: outside the blob the frame before and the frame after differ by 1.3 to 2 grey levels in every colour over the whole screen (the frames either side are identical to the bit; strip rows in r58-tile-swap-strip.jpg), once, at the frame where the red push's scale passes 255 (read each frame: 232.3 at 805 ms, 255.7 at 822 ms; the filter's map has a neutral byte of 128, not 127.5, so every push is shifted by 0.00196 x its scale in pixels, and at a scale of 255 that is half a pixel: the displacement map's nearest sample takes a whole pixel). It is not made by the tile ladder: it was at the same moment with early steps of 0.025 and 0.0125, and with the peak cut from 8.55% to 7% of the height (red scale 229, under 255) the same swap reads 1.12, 1.17 and 1.26 in the three runs (counter-experiment, not committed).",
  "since": "R58.1: the lens of R54 and R56 had a red scale under 255 at every size; the hero's liquid at 150% has 280 at 1440 by 900 (2 x 1.3 x 77 px x 1.4), 262 at 390 by 844 and 349 at the 96 px cap.",
  "not_fixed": "Out of this round's scope (no new primitive; the owner picked the strength): options are a smaller red share (a peak cut to 7% of the height clears it at 900 high but changes the look), a bias cancelled by one feOffset per push (three more primitives in each filter, a per-frame cost), or accepting one half-pixel step of the page in the third of a second the bend ramps in. For the controller to rule."
 },
 "early_step_history": {
  "0.05 (R58.1)": "not measurable: the first audit's labels were wrong. The swaps of the early tiles move the band by up to half a step (0.025 = 21 px at 1440 by 900).",
  "0.025 (first run of the fix round)": "early swaps (fronts -0.04 to 0.18) at ratio 1.2 to 4.4, 6 swaps a run over 1.5 against the control's 0.9 to 1.1: the brief's fallback was not enough.",
  "0.0125 (this record)": "early swaps (fronts -0.14 to 0.2) 0.04 to 1.3 apart from tile 23: the fallback of Ruling R129."
 },
